From f2ad97a376b0cd50b6be930e2d4f465fdd63386a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mutouyuguo <yaq-1944@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:37:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(storage): co-purchase second-hop aggregation pushdown
 (prototype)

Add a group_by_dst mode to GetNeighbors: storage filters the edge predicate, counts dst(edge) per part and returns (item, partial_count) instead of per-buyer edge lists. graphd recognizes GO | GROUP BY dst, COUNT(1), threads the flag through ExpandAll, and sums the partial counts in AggregateExecutor; Filter/Project/HashInnerJoin pass grouped rows through.

Verified on a single-node cluster with 4 buyers / 5 items: query returns a=2, b=3, c=3, d=1 and logs show GroupByDstNode + ExpandAll pushdown. Prototype scope: one OUT join pattern, wildcard edge type scan, no affinity LOCAL_CHAIN, no local TopN.
